### Pro1X: up to kernel 7.1.0-pro1x.7 every resume of the sound card popped
### in the loudspeaker (codec and amplifier power-up), so the card stayed open
### for 300 s after a sound instead of PulseAudio's 5 s, about 100 mA and
### 400 interrupts a second meanwhile. Kernel patch 0026 (pro1x.8 and later)
### orders the amplifiers after the codec's PA; those kernels have
### /sys/module/snd_soc_aw87339/parameters/on_delay_ms. With such a kernel
### the card suspends after 3 s of silence (the N9 used 1-5 s), with an older
### one after 300 s.
### Still a pop with the new kernel: touch /etc/pulse/pro1x-suspend-300 and
### restart PulseAudio (back to 300 s; remove the file to undo).
.ifexists module-suspend-on-idle.so
unload-module module-suspend-on-idle
.endif
.ifexists /sys/module/snd_soc_aw87339/parameters/on_delay_ms
load-module module-suspend-on-idle timeout=3
.else
load-module module-suspend-on-idle timeout=300
.endif
.ifexists /etc/pulse/pro1x-suspend-300
unload-module module-suspend-on-idle
load-module module-suspend-on-idle timeout=300
.endif
